               have positive impacts on the environment by local natural
               resource management authorities. A rigorous measure of complex
               land management practice is developed in relation to native
               vegetation, weeds, soil, stock, and perennials. The model was
               able to predict 52\% of the variance in complex behaviour.
               Contextual factors, values, attitudes, and norms are identified
               as important predictors. Results suggest skills and abilities,
