  volume    =  115,
  pages     = "276--284",
  abstract  = "Much research has been devoted to identify the conditions under
               which selection favours flexible individuals or genotypes that
               are able to modify their growth, development and behaviour in
               response to environmental cues, to unravel the mechanisms of
               plasticity and to explore its influence on patterns of diversity
               among individuals, populations and species. The consequences of
